---
title: Coffee Cake or Caramel Rolls
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Good Morning, Morning Glory!
cook time: 25 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@dry yeast{1%pkg}
@sugar{0.5%tsp}
@warm water{0.5%cup}
@milk{1%cup}
@shortening{0.25%cup}
@sugar{0.25%cup}
@salt{1%tsp}
@egg{1%beaten}
@flour{4%cups}

Let yeast, 1/2 tsp sugar, and warm water sit. Scald milk and add shortening, 1/4 cup sugar, salt, beaten egg and flour. Mix all ingredients together and let raise until double.

==Coffee Cake==
Put in 2 pie pans and spread with @soft butter. Put on @sliced apples and sprinkle with @sugar and @cinnamon. Let raise until double.

==Caramel Rolls==
Roll dough out VERY thin and spread with @soft butter. Sprinkle with @cinnamon and @brown sugar. Roll up and cut. Put @brown sugar (and @pecan nuts, if desired) and a few sprinkles of @cream or milk in bottom of pan. Place cut pieces in pan and let raise until double.

Bake at 375 degrees for about 25 minutes or until nicely brown.
